{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgyoStfeKzb16MYJxoqQ9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The flag keeps old function names working. According to the docstring in `scripts/build.py`, `--legacy-imports` adds a file `pkg/_legacy.py` to the built bundle that contains one line:\n\n```python\nfrom .core import group_totals as sum_by, parse_amount as to_decimal\n```\n\nSo `sum_by` and `to_decimal`, the names used before 1.0, keep working as aliases for `group_totals` and `parse_amount`. Without the flag, code that still imports the old names breaks on upgrade.\n\nI can't tell from the repo whether anyone still needs it:\n- Nothing else in the repo uses `_legacy`, `sum_by` or `to_decimal`: not the tests, the README, the changelog, or `pkg/` itself.\n- The changelog never mentions the rename or a deprecation, and the git history doesn't say why the flag exists. The only commit that touches it is `Release 1.3.2`, which looks like where the history starts.\n\nSo it isn't dead code: it changes what users get. Whether it's cruft depends on whether downstream users still import the old names, and that's outside the repo. Dropping the flag would be a breaking change for those users, so it should get a changelog entry and probably wait for a major version or a deprecation notice.\n\nI haven't changed anything. Do you want me to remove it from the runbook and the build script, or add a deprecation note first?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":160,"cache_read_input_tokens":21268,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":160},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-40>","timestamp":"2026-11-12T22